            <ArticleTitle>Updating a 12-year experience with arrest and reversal therapy for coronary heart disease (an overdue requiem for palliative cardiology).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>339-41, A8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery disease is essentially nonexistent in cultures whose nutrition assures cholesterol levels &lt;150 mg/dl. Patients with advanced coronary artery disease may abolish disease progression through a plant-based diet and cholesterol-lowering medication to achieve and maintain a total cholesterol &lt;150 mg/dl.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
